  "name": "flame_wisp_spark",
  "description": "lit blue flame veils and strands crossing on a deep blue ground, strewn with gold star sparks",
  "reference": {
    "image": "cosmic-forces-25.jpg",
    "folder": "fractal-drive-sync/style-refs",
    "made_with": "an Apophysis-style flame (signed exoteric.roach.org), 2560x1600"
  },
  "suggested_colormap": "flame_wisp_spark",
  "reuses": [
    "the stripe average (field `stripe`) through flame_veil_blue's `view`s, six of them on a golden-angle spiral plus the frame's own: per loop a soft veil (density 3, power 2) and fine strands (density 10, power 10), screened: crossing strands filling the frame",
    "glow_filaments' falloff hair with a halo, in gold, on the set's `de` through the frame and three of the views: the star sparks",
    "the tone pass with log_density, at the reference's median and p10"
  ],
  "adds": [],
  "notes": [
    "Added: nothing new to the engine: seven loops' stripe crests through the blue map, and the star sparks as glow_filaments' falloff hair with a gold halo on the set's `de` through the frame and one view, the tone pass.",
    "Fitted: sparks through four loops covered a dendrite seat in gold filigree and read p90 0.71 against 0.56 on a dense seat; two loops at lower opacity left them sparks.",
    "Lessons: item 032 brought five flame references whose look is fine strands and wisps filling the frame (commons_Waves_Apophysis_Fractal_Flame.jpg, convocation-dragons-25.jpg, cosmic-forces-25.jpg, creeping-frost-25.jpg, deaths-icy-hand-25.jpg), after item 028's flame_veil_* scored 2/5 as a few broad sheets. **The strands are the stripe average, not the smooth count**: sheets cut from the smooth count follow its level lines, which nest round the set as rings (through six views at period 0.25 they drew a tunnel of ellipses), while the stripe average's crests run along the orbit's field lines, across the level lines, as fine as its density asks; raised to power 10 only the crests light, and seven loops (the frame and six views on a golden-angle spiral, turned, scaled 0.8 to 1.9 and shifted up to 0.55 frame widths) cross their strands over the whole frame. Under them the same field at density 3 and power 2 is the soft veil. Far from the set the crests run as near-straight rays (ten views at density 8 read as a fan of straight lines); nearer the set they curl, so the strands curl most on seats with set in the frame. **Wisps need far field, as veils did**: of the forty-seat gallery draw (`style scout --n 40`) seven showed the wisps and the rest were filled by lace (the set's own hair floods it), so the locations are item 028's hand-placed shallow seats (its measurement: far-field share median 0.285 over 40 gallery seats, 0.544 over 40 hand seats) with those seven gallery seats (step 4's exception). A full-size frame of seven loops took about two minutes at six threads, a parabolic (r 1.0) or phoenix seat over four; round one is drawn at --draft."
  ],
